{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123255","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123255/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123255/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123255/events","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123255","id":5365970982,"node_id":"I_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABP9Y4Jg","number":123255,"title":"Causing a shader compilation error and fixing it causes RenderingDevice error","user":{"login":"mFieldHouses","id":131540025,"node_id":"U_kgDOB9ckOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131540025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses","html_url":"https://github.com/mFieldHouses","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mFieldHouses/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-09-06T15:40:43Z","updated_at":"2026-09-06T20:43:22Z","closed_at":"2026-09-06T15:48:01Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nIssue found starting from v4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee], including v4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4], v4.7.stable.official [5b4e0cb0f] and v4.7.2.stable.official [ed1daf0bf],\n\nissue was **not** found on v4.3.stable.official [77dcf97d8]\n\n### System information\n\n Using Forward+ renderer, GPU: GTX1060 Mobile, POP_OS 22.04 LTS. CPU: Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-6700HQ CPU @ 2.60GHz\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen causing a shader compilation error, and subsequently fixing it, the editor throws a single editor multiple times (RenderingDevice: Attempted to free invalid ID: #). In a fresh project, this is usually 5 times, but in another project of mine, this was thrown something like 20-30 times.\n\n<img width=\"1349\" height=\"367\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/45a3736c-f04c-4c68-b8d2-755fe647e9a3\" />\n\nI could not find any logs related to this project.\n\nIn my case, it will display a single error repeated a few times like in the screenshot above.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create any project with the Forward+ renderer\n2. Create a 3D scene\n3. Add a MeshInstance3D to the scene, pick any mesh and assign a ShaderMaterial to it\n4. Create a shader for the ShaderMaterial, and add something like `ALBEDO = vec3(1.0, 0.0, 0.0);` to its fragment() function to make sure it works.\n5. Remove the semicolon in the line you just added, or cause any other shader compilation error.\n6. Fix the compilation error, and check the editor output.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.co